# Architecture Boundaries

## The four layers

```
src/app/api/**/route.ts       ← API Layer
src/lib/services/*.service.ts ← Service Layer (business logic)
src/lib/db/models/*.ts        ← Model Layer (data schema)
src/app/**/*.tsx              ← UI Layer
src/components/**/*.tsx       ← UI Layer
src/hooks/api/*.ts            ← Client Data Layer
```

## What each layer may import

### API Layer (`src/app/api/`)

May import from:
- `src/lib/auth/guards` — `withAuth`, `withRole`, `withAgent`, `withAdmin`, `withOptionalAuth`
- `src/lib/validators/*.server.ts` — Zod schemas for request validation
- `src/lib/services/*.service.ts` — business logic execution
- `src/lib/api/response.ts` — response helpers
- `src/lib/db/connect` — only for routes that bypass services (rare; justify in a comment)

Must NOT import from:
- `src/lib/db/models/` directly (use a service instead — except auth routes which legitimately access User)
- `src/components/`
- `src/hooks/`

### Service Layer (`src/lib/services/`)

May import from:
- `src/lib/db/connect`
- `src/lib/db/models/`
- `src/lib/config/`
- Other services when composing logic
- `src/lib/email/` for sending emails as part of a workflow

Must NOT import from:
- `next/server`, `next/navigation`, or any Next.js module
- `src/app/`
- `src/components/`
- `src/hooks/`
- `src/lib/api/` (response helpers are for API routes, not services; services throw errors)

### Model Layer (`src/lib/db/models/`)

May import from:
- Other models in `src/lib/db/models/` (refs only)
- `src/lib/config/` (for constants like `UNIVERSITY_IDS`, `PLATFORM_CONFIG`)
- `mongoose`
- `bcryptjs` (User model only)

Must NOT import from anything else. Models are the deepest layer.

### UI Layer (`src/app/**/*.tsx`, `src/components/**/*.tsx`)

May import from:
- `src/hooks/api/` — **only** way to fetch/mutate data on the client
- `src/lib/api/types.ts` — type definitions for API responses
- `src/lib/utils/` — pure utility functions
- `src/lib/config/env.ts` — constants like `PLATFORM_CONFIG` (client-safe fields only)
- `src/components/` — other components
- `src/types/` — shared type definitions

Must NOT import from:
- `src/lib/db/` — server-only, causes build failures in client bundles
- `src/lib/services/` — server-only
- `src/lib/auth/guards.ts` — server-only
- `src/lib/auth/jwt.ts` — server-only

### Client Data Layer (`src/hooks/api/`)

May import from:
- `src/lib/api/client.ts` — Axios instance
- `src/lib/api/types.ts` — response types
- `src/lib/query/keys.ts` — query key factory
- `@tanstack/react-query`

Must NOT import from:
- `src/lib/db/`
- `src/lib/services/`

## Business logic placement

Business logic belongs **exclusively** in `src/lib/services/*.service.ts`. This includes:

- Ownership checks (e.g., "does this agentId own this listing?")
- State transitions (e.g., approving a payment → updating unlockedListingIds)
- Data privacy filtering (e.g., `toPublicListing()` vs `toUnlockedListing()`)
- Cross-entity logic (e.g., counting a user's unlocked listings)

API routes must be thin: validate input → call service → return response.

```typescript
// Correct — thin API route
export const POST = withAgent(async (request, context) => {
  const body = await request.json();
  const validation = createListingSchema.safeParse(body);
  if (!validation.success) return validationErrorResponse(validation.error);
  const listing = await listingsService.createListing(context.user.userId, validation.data);
  return successResponse({ listing }, 201);
});

// Wrong — business logic leaking into API route
export const POST = withAgent(async (request, context) => {
  const body = await request.json();
  const existing = await Listing.findOne({ title: body.title }); // direct DB in route
  if (existing) return conflictResponse('Title already exists');   // business rule in route
  ...
});
```

## Auth guard usage — no exceptions

Every API route that requires authentication must be wrapped in a guard HOC. No inline cookie reading or manual JWT verification in route handlers.

```typescript
// Correct
export const DELETE = withAgent(handler);
export const GET = withOptionalAuth(handler);

// Wrong — never do this in a route handler
const token = request.cookies.get('access_token');
const payload = await verifyToken(token.value);
```

Available guards and their role requirements:

| Guard | Allowed roles |
|-------|--------------|
| `withAuth` | Any authenticated user |
| `withUser` | Any authenticated user (alias for withAuth) |
| `withAgent` | `agent` only |
| `withAdmin` | `admin` only |
| `withAgentOrAdmin` | `agent` or `admin` |
| `withRole([...])` | Custom role list |
| `withOptionalAuth` | Unauthenticated or authenticated (provides context if authenticated) |

